AWS S3 Lifecycle policies
Use Case: Streaming Service Data Management
Day 1 - 30: Store new data in S3 Standard for frequent access.
>>This allows analysts, ML pipelines, and reporting tools to access fresh data quickly.
Day 31 - 90: Transition to S3 Standard-IA (Infrequent Access).
>>Data accessed occasionally for analytics or audits is stored at a lower cost.
After 90 Days: Move to S3 Glacier Flexible Retrieval for archival purposes.
>>Retain data for compliance or long-term analysis, with occasional access.
After 2 Years: Move to S3 Glacier Deep Archive.
>>This is for data that must be kept for regulatory purposes but is rarely accessed.
After 7 Years: Delete the data.
>>In compliance with data retention policies, objects no longer needed are removed to save costs
