AWS S3 Version
Enabling Versioning: When you enable versioning on a bucket, every new object uploaded will have a unique version ID.
Overwriting Objects: If an object is overwritten, a new version is created, and the previous version remains in the bucket.
Deleting Objects: When an object is deleted, S3 doesn't remove the object data. Instead, it inserts a delete marker3. The delete marker becomes the current version of the object.
Restoring Objects: If you delete the delete marker, the object is restored to its previous version.
---------------

